{
  "tema": 8392,
  "slug": "lo-neutro",
  "titulo": "Neuter lo to refer to a clause, verb, adjective or adverb",
  "subtitulo": "—¿Estás cansada? —Sí, lo estoy.",
  "foto": "t08.jpg",
  "regla": "Lo can stand for a whole idea, an action, or an adjective already mentioned: Tenías que disculparte pero no lo hiciste. —¿Es guapa? —Sí, lo es. It never changes (never la / los), and it's required where English drops it.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Lo** can replace something already said that isn't a specific noun:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "usos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "forma": "a clause / idea",
              "texto": "**¿Lo recordarás?** (= that grandpa's pill is at 12)"
            },
            {
              "forma": "an action",
              "texto": "**Tenías que disculparte, pero no lo hiciste.**"
            },
            {
              "forma": "an adjective or adverb with ser / estar / parecer",
              "texto": "**No parece contento, pero lo está.** **—¿Estás bien? —Sí, lo estoy.**"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Lo** never changes, even for a feminine or plural adjective: **—¿Es guapa? —Sí, lo es.**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "It's **required**: English says _Yes, I am_; Spanish needs **sí, lo estoy**, or simply **sí**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **lo** = _it, so, that_, standing in for anything that isn't a thing."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Tenías que disculparte, pero no ==lo== hiciste.",
              "en": "You were supposed to apologize, but you didn't."
            },
            {
              "es": "Sabes que la pastilla del abuelo es a las doce. ¿==Lo== vas a recordar?",
              "en": "You know grandpa's pill is at twelve. Will you remember?"
            },
            {
              "es": "No parece muy contento, pero yo sé que ==lo== está.",
              "en": "He doesn't look very happy, but I know he is."
            },
            {
              "es": "—¿Estás bien, mi amor? —Sí, ==lo== estoy, ma.",
              "en": "—Are you OK, honey? —Yes, I am, Mom."
            },
            {
              "es": "—Dicen que la chava es muy guapa. —No, no ==lo== es.",
              "en": "—They say the girl is really pretty. —No, she isn't."
            },
            {
              "es": "—¿Son hermanos? —Sí, ==lo== son.",
              "en": "—Are they siblings? —Yes, they are."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
